<td id="S5.T6.fig2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><span id="S5.T6.fig2.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.6</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.7 </span>Evaluation on General Capabilities</h3>

<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the general capabilities of the model equipped HIRE, using LLaVA-1.5-7B as a representative model on two challenging benchmarks: MME <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yin et al., 2024a</a>)</cite> and SEED-Bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023a</a>)</cite>.As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 5.7 Evaluation on General Capabilities ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Hallucination-aware Intermediate Representation Edit in Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, it can be observed that our method preserves the model’s general capabilities on these benchmarks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Comparison of general capabilities on MME and SEED-Bench.</figcaption>
