</figure>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We further present evaluation results on the GQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hudson and Manning, 2019</a>)</cite> and A-OKVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schwenk et al., 2022</a>)</cite> datasets under the POPE benchmark in Table <a href="#A4.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ D.6 Evaluating Generalization Ability on Diverse Models and Datasets ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Hallucination-aware Intermediate Representation Edit in Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, comparing against previously reported results from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Woo et al. (2024)</a></cite>. Our method achieves consistent improvements in both accuracy and F1 score across these datasets.</p>
</div>
